# Variable template for deploying BloodHound CE on lab58.
# Fallback for running `docker compose up -d` by hand only — the real Komodo deploy writes
# bloodhound-ce/.env itself from komodo/stacks/bloodhound-ce.toml (see CLAUDE.md's "Secrets
# via Komodo Variables"); editing values here has no effect on that path.
# Docs: https://bloodhound.specterops.io/

## Image versions are pinned directly in docker-compose.yml (not here) so Renovate can
## track and bump them — see the note in CLAUDE.md about deploy-only Renovate coverage.

POSTGRES_USER=bloodhound
POSTGRES_DB=bloodhound
## CHANGE before deploying — generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme

NEO4J_USER=neo4j
## CHANGE before deploying — generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`. Also gates whether
## it's ever safe to publish Neo4j's own ports to the LAN (see docker-compose.yml).
NEO4J_SECRET=changeme

## No env var needed for the admin login: BloodHound randomizes it on first boot and
## prints it to `docker compose logs bloodhound` ("Initial Password Set To: ...").
